# GO_CONTRACT_ONLY — I04.var06 return-complete transfer classification

Decision: **GO_CONTRACT_ONLY** for the RO prospective contract `tmp/i04-var06-prospective-v100-20261008-01/contract.json`, 10,668 bytes/SHA-256 `87a22902a86bde7d9d668d816830bd5b4b87ee6b6c4d6f289bf94190f83b90a2`, and explanatory `contract.md`, 5,589 bytes/SHA-256 `a68a8c21bb83ec4b5e2a2ea2a7fb5faef0819ae6a14329197e2e8726653e8036`. This permits separate local construction of `I04-var06-return-complete-transfer-v1.0.0` only after root release. The package and classification scratch were absent at audit. No native run, accepted-parent checker replay, model source change, or report export is authorized by this GO.

The independent RO contract audit `tmp/i04-var06-independent-contract-audit-v101-20261008.py` is 6,169 bytes/SHA-256 `74d9feea302aa8922f105b35a0dd9fda17a71a620d9f6c083effcf4e93164012`. Its original root capture `tmp/i04-var09-root-review-proofs-v100-20261008/i04-var06-v100-contract-audit-20261008T151010606438Z-a34ce8c9/receipt.json` is 1,366 bytes/SHA-256 `3d56ea2fb6a68de93be3e8d8ad257d4ea5d2dfe40c701a90cfc1fdfedafcf167`: actual integer exit 0, empty original stderr, stable capture/auditor pins; original stdout 69 bytes/SHA-256 `bd9c4a4ffccd02104bcb749c95d6fae182bfbc94094a3715d5d4b6645f98b3ad` reports `PASS_I04_VAR06_CONTRACT_ONLY 15 24 76 117 103 selected2 zero_native`.

The prospective classification is limited to the accepted I04.var01 BETWEEN original: a source-frozen h8.5 one-aircraft transfer request, first mission assignment of physical ID0, h10 turnround/return/ready followed by ready decrement and transfer-out, h10.5 target transfer-in and ready increase, and a later distinct mission at h19–22. The original log is 8,158 bytes/SHA-256 `e9c2bbc20a9496c1ce72f3e4c2806c94d1a52ab8ee409a37ea790bc98eca1c8f`, 117 lines/103 timed. It does not print the request at h8.5. The input has one exact `SystemTransfer` row with `TFDT=0.5`; the selected SystemResults rows for `[10,10.5)` and `[10.5,11)` corroborate ready/available counts 1→2. The earlier parent 439/439 GO remains inherited provenance, not a new full-report acceptance. The installed manual is a local-only exact hash pin, not copied into the package.

Construction must keep all 24 accepted raw originals mandatory at unchanged bytes and original filesystem attributes; they are historically writable. A later unique ignored proof directory may hold byte-identical read-only copies for the new classifier. The new independent reader must be separate from the author implementation, consume the full fixed 117/103 log under a strict outer SHA gate, track physical inner aircraft IDs separately from outer station descriptors, maintain ready/assignment/transit/mission/total-fleet conservation through both missions, and reject predeclared private semantic clones beneath that SHA gate. Exact 15 parent source and 76 dependency disk/Git pair pins, catalog500 distinct CRLF/LF identity and typed prefix, and selected report type/row/time checks remain required before bounded acceptance.

An earlier v100 auditor source, 6,048 bytes/SHA-256 `7a062eed5c709f4b6fe7b63505d31cc24bb80b779102da94c33c291c1b8c8c8c`, failed once in a decoded-only local development run because it assumed the h10 `System ready` line was unique. The fixed accepted log prints that line twice. Its source and limitation are preserved externally in `tmp/i04-var06-independent-contract-auditor-development-20261008.md` SHA-256 `90868fbf0ec96b25440c09f65cca44ba94079f0f62c61573b628459ae05ddfdf`; no original binary failure receipt is claimed. The v101 original captured PASS supersedes that false predicate without changing accepted evidence.

Any maintenance-completion, positive-turnround-duration, simultaneous new-mission priority, general aircraft-selection, implicit-unit, IN/OUT, GUI, performance, cross-engine or whole-I04.var06 claim remains outside this contract. A later classification and publication require their own independent source, semantic, custody, content, staged and remote gates.
